-- Executes SPIR-V compute shaders on an available Vulkan device.
public define device as opaque.
public define buffer as opaque.
public define kernel as opaque.

public use "vulkan" function available giving boolean.
public use "vulkan" function count giving unsigned.
public use "vulkan" function open giving failable pointer to device.
public use "vulkan" function select(index unsigned) giving failable pointer to device.
public use "vulkan" function name(device pointer to device) giving failable text.
public use "vulkan" function reserve(device pointer to device, size unsigned) giving failable pointer to buffer.
-- Host-visible coherent buffers remain mapped for their full lifetime.
public use "vulkan" function upload(buffer pointer to buffer, source sequence of constant byte) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function download(buffer pointer to buffer, destination sequence of byte) giving failable nothing.
-- Code is SPIR-V. Group is the shader's declared local size.
public use "vulkan" function compile(device pointer to device, code sequence of constant byte, bindings unsigned, group unsigned) giving failable pointer to kernel.
public use "vulkan" function bind(kernel pointer to kernel, index unsigned, buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function launch(kernel pointer to kernel, count unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function dispatch(kernel pointer to kernel, count unsigned, group unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function plane(kernel pointer to kernel, x unsigned, y unsigned, columns unsigned, rows unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function volume(kernel pointer to kernel, x unsigned, y unsigned, z unsigned, columns unsigned, rows unsigned, layers unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function finish(device pointer to device) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function discard(kernel pointer to kernel) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function dispose(buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable nothing.
public use "vulkan" function close(device pointer to device) giving failable nothing.
